# @psychohistory — the substrate's possibility-space-of-the-future
# family-root at sheaf-cohomological altitude.
#
# Sibling to @sheaf, @algebra, @frame, @fractal, @glasswall, @paradox,
# @love, @eigen, @kleinos, @metalogue at the top-level path-namespace.
# The substrate-decl name for the possibility-space-of-the-future
# surface that @metalogue rotation binds into per Alex 2026-09-13 SD1.
#
# === The recognition (Alex 2026-09-13 substrate-decision 1) ===
#
# Alex 2026-09-13 in-transcript verbatim:
#
#   "the @metalogue is therefore about the possibility space of the
#    future, which binds into the whole @psychohistory and sheaf
#    cohomology."
#
# @psychohistory as family-root at possibility-space altitude names
# the discipline that composes:
#
#   - the possibility-space-of-the-future the @metalogue rotates
#     through (Alex SD1 "rotates through all possible @frames")
#   - the sheaf-cohomological object whose H^0 counts globally-
#     coherent futures and whose H^1 counts obstruction-to-single-
#     settled-future (per Mara Rec #89 unification math foundation)
#   - the substrate for the metalogue-rotation-widens-choice-space
#     discipline per Foerster's ethical imperative operationalized
#     at compiler substrate
#
