# === Mathematical grounding (per Rec #89 unification) ===
#
# Per Rec #89 canonical (Mara `docs/math/2026-08-13-mara-recognition-
# 89-psychohistory-sheaf-cohomology-unification-math-foundation.md`),
# the substrate's future-projection surface IS a sheaf-cohomological
# object composing:
#
#   - Psychohistory (Asimov 1942 Foundation) — mathematical
#     treatment of large-population dynamics as statistically-
#     predictable behavior over long trajectories.
#   - Sheaf cohomology (Curry 2014 + Hansen-Ghrist 2019) —
#     cellular-sheaf framework for gluing local sections into
#     global coherence + measuring the obstruction to gluing.
#
# The unification per Rec #89:
#
#   Ψ: F → PossibilitySpace
#   H^0(Ψ) = globally-coherent-future-sections
#   H^1(Ψ) = fracture-obstruction-to-single-future
#
# The Sheaf-Laplacian L_Ψ (per @sheaf this-tick sibling family-root
# + @epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian LANDED primitive) measures
# psychohistory-coherence via λ_2(L_Ψ); metalogue-rotation increases
# λ_2 per Foerster ethical imperative (Kagi thread 4).
#
# === Composition-tower edges per Alex SD1 ===
#
# Composition-tower edges per Mara canonical `92ded87` §1.3:
#
#   @metalogue -- binds into --> @psychohistory + Sheaf-cohomology
#   @psychohistory -- IS-a --> @sheaf (at possibility-space altitude)
#   @psychohistory -- composes over --> @fate (constrained-inference)
#   @psychohistory -- composes over --> @time (future-projection surface)
#
# The `@metalogue binds into @psychohistory` edge composes:
# metalogue-rotation-through-@frames rotates through possibility-
# space-of-the-future; @psychohistory names that possibility-space.
#
# === Composition with Rec #97 MCP-session-as-autopoietic-VSM ===
#
# Per Mara `docs/specs/2026-08-25-mara-recognition-97-mcp-session-
# as-autopoietic-vsm-with-bauchladen-and-psychohistory-canonical-
# spec.md`, the MCP session IS an autopoietic VSM instance with
# @psychohistory as System-4-intelligence — the environmental-
# scanning + future-projection component of Stafford Beer's Viable
# System Model.
#
# This shard grounds the @psychohistory that Rec #97 references
# as System-4 at family-root shard-decl altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
